# cycle/requests.jsonl — the FLEET & EQUIPMENT record's inbound door. Append-only.
#
# ⭐ THIS IS TRACK B's DOOR, NOT THE MOM-CYCLE'S. Read BACKLOG.md's opening:
# Fernwood carries TWO PRODUCTS in one repo — Track A, Mom's field journal, and
# Track B, Paul's fleet & equipment tracker. Different users, tone, cadence and
# definition of done. The mom-cycle (MOM-CYCLE-MAP.md) is Track A's loop and has
# NO BEAT for a vehicle record. Track B has no loop at all.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. On 2026-08-28 two vehicle facts surfaced from a comms sweep —
# two LMC Truck orders addressed to the house instead of the gatehouse, and a
# Golf GTI service visit with no serviceHistory entry. `ask-cycle.py` REFUSED
# both, correctly: Fernwood's only declared loop is the mom-cycle and neither ask
# belonged in it. They reached BACKLOG.md because a session remembered to put
# them there. This door is so the next one does not depend on remembering.
# `demand.py` had both logged as DEMONSTRATED DEMAND — 2 asks, no door.
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE. A fact about a vehicle, a part, a piece of equipment, a
# service event or a delivery address that the Fernwood record has wrong, missing
# or unverified. ⚠️ The parts record is known wrong in BOTH directions
# ([[reference_parts_record_under_reports]]): it has under-reported what Paul
# OWNS and over-reported what he ORDERED. Absence is not evidence, and neither is
# a stated order — clear an order with an ORDER NUMBER.
#
#   python3 ~/.claude/tools/ask-cycle.py fernwood-fleet "<the fact + its evidence>" --from <project>
#
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE. Anything about Mom, her feedback, the journal, the
# viewer, or her asks — that is Track A and it rides the mom-cycle. Filing it
# here puts it where no beat reads it.
#
# ⚠️ NOTHING SWEEPS THIS FILE ON A CADENCE. Track B has no loop, so an entry is
# read when fleet work is next opened. A durable inbox, not an alarm; a
# time-sensitive fact also belongs on BACKLOG.md, which stays the canonical
# surface for Fernwood open work.
#
# Shape (one JSON object per line):
#   {"from":"security","what":"LMC order W7610655 shipped to the house, belonged at the gatehouse","opened":"2026-08-28"}
{"from": "photo-organizer", "what": "GTI 2026-07-21 — TEN photographs of repairs Paul says he did himself, Paul-ruled by voice 2026-08-28 as observed:gti-2016:repair:2026-07-21 (photo-organizer sweep 120, reports/project-review-never-reviewed-bursts.answers.json). His words: '76 through 85 [a]re repairs that I did on the GTI'. This repo's own inbound-door commit records that ask-cycle refused 'the GTI service visit with no serviceHistory entry' on 8/28 — this is dated photographic evidence for that gap. ⚠️ It evidences that work happened on that date and nothing more: WHAT was repaired is unread, and the VLM captions must not be used to say.", "opened": "2026-08-28"}
